1
00:00:18,151 --> 00:00:19,684
I already called Mr. Dencio.

2
00:00:19,684 --> 00:00:20,919
Just ride home with us.

3
00:00:20,919 --> 00:00:22,453
I'll take the tricycle home.

4
00:00:22,453 --> 00:00:23,991
There are no more tricycles.

5
00:00:23,991 --> 00:00:26,347
I'm sure there are a lot of tricycles
on the highway.

6
00:00:26,347 --> 00:00:28,626
- I'll wait there.
- Are you sure?

7
00:00:28,626 --> 00:00:29,861
It's dark there.

8
00:00:29,861 --> 00:00:32,530
He said he was on his way home.

9
00:00:32,530 --> 00:00:34,465
And Florence is with him.

10
00:00:34,465 --> 00:00:35,550
They're together?

11
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:37,101
Why, Bro, is there a problem?

12
00:00:37,101 --> 00:00:41,612
What's with the Ferells,
and you really want to protect me?

13
00:00:41,612 --> 00:00:43,792
What's this, messianic complex,

14
00:00:43,792 --> 00:00:47,879
or all of you can't help
but be a Prince Charming?

15
00:00:47,879 --> 00:00:50,684
Do you all want to save a damsel in distress?

16
00:00:50,684 --> 00:00:53,318
It's not a weakness to ask for help.

17
00:00:53,318 --> 00:00:55,214
Sometimes, that's the way things are.

18
00:00:55,214 --> 00:00:58,289
We need others so we can bounce back.

19
00:00:58,289 --> 00:01:02,198
Sometimes, you have to be true
to what you're feeling.

20
00:01:02,198 --> 00:01:04,855
Don't be scared to show it to others.

21
00:01:04,855 --> 00:01:06,931
You said that we should be true to ourselves.

22
00:01:06,931 --> 00:01:08,666
Well, then I'll be true too.

23
00:01:08,666 --> 00:01:11,105
I know
so you don't have to look at me that way.

24
00:01:11,105 --> 00:01:12,534
And besides, I know I'm not your type

25
00:01:12,534 --> 00:01:15,106
especially when I saw
your ex-girlfriend Antonia.

26
00:01:15,106 --> 00:01:16,641
There's a huge difference between us.

27
00:01:16,641 --> 00:01:19,230
If you compare Antonia with me,
that's heaven and earth.

28
00:01:19,230 --> 00:01:20,159
I'm the earth part.

29
00:01:20,159 --> 00:01:21,701
That's heaven and earth.
You too, you're heaven.

30
00:01:21,701 --> 00:01:22,767
Heaven, heaven, heaven...

31
00:01:22,767 --> 00:01:24,284
that's you and Antonia, you're both heaven

32
00:01:24,284 --> 00:01:26,309
while I'm the earth
and you really won't fall for me.

33
00:01:26,309 --> 00:01:29,354
And besides, how would you fall
for your crude cook?

34
00:01:29,354 --> 00:01:30,722
That's impossible.

35
00:01:30,722 --> 00:01:32,512
Why would it be impossible?

36
00:01:32,512 --> 00:01:34,359
You're not difficult to like.

37
00:01:34,359 --> 00:01:36,961
Hello, Lina, I'm here on the third floor,
where are you?

38
00:01:36,961 --> 00:01:38,529
Guys, have you seen Florence?

39
00:01:38,529 --> 00:01:40,665
I know she has a class right now.

40
00:01:40,665 --> 00:01:43,356
But I passed by her classroom
and she was not there.

41
00:01:43,356 --> 00:01:45,124
Lina!

42
00:01:47,838 --> 00:01:52,243
Congrats, you followed our instructions.

43
00:01:52,243 --> 00:01:55,345
Finally, you're learning.

44
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:57,448
Is anyone there?

45
00:01:57,448 --> 00:01:59,330
Kindly open the door.

46
00:01:59,330 --> 00:02:00,618
Hello?

47
00:02:00,618 --> 00:02:01,525
Lina!

48
00:02:01,525 --> 00:02:03,519
I'm just looking for Nero.

49
00:02:03,519 --> 00:02:04,921
Have you seen him?

50
00:02:04,921 --> 00:02:06,322
Oh, Nero.

51
00:02:06,322 --> 00:02:08,123
He's just there.

52
00:02:34,918 --> 00:02:36,819
Florence!

53
00:04:00,770 --> 00:04:02,637
Drink some more.

54
00:04:05,141 --> 00:04:07,075
I'm okay now.

55
00:04:11,247 --> 00:04:13,516
We have a clinic.

56
00:04:13,516 --> 00:04:15,584
Do you want me to take you there?

57
00:04:16,685 --> 00:04:18,620
I'm okay now.

58
00:04:20,756 --> 00:04:25,127
Thank you for saving me earlier.

59
00:04:25,127 --> 00:04:28,230
I thought I'd be locked there forever.

60
00:04:31,133 --> 00:04:33,869
Are you sure they didn't
do anything else to you?

61
00:04:33,869 --> 00:04:36,439
They just locked you inside the room?

62
00:04:36,439 --> 00:04:38,007
Yes.

63
00:04:38,007 --> 00:04:42,015
I just had a panic attack
because I'm scared of the dark.

64
00:04:42,015 --> 00:04:46,452
That's really my biggest phobia
and what I hate most.

65
00:04:47,383 --> 00:04:50,919
Maybe a traumatic event happened to you
when you were young.

66
00:04:52,221 --> 00:04:57,225
Maybe I just get scared easily.

67
00:05:06,876 --> 00:05:10,246
How did you find out where I was earlier?

68
00:05:12,047 --> 00:05:13,848
Where is she?

69
00:05:17,613 --> 00:05:20,783
If you won't tell me where she is...

70
00:05:20,783 --> 00:05:23,018
you'll have to fight with me.

71
00:05:31,865 --> 00:05:35,269
Camille and Aira won't stop bothering me.

72
00:05:35,269 --> 00:05:37,522
Do you want us to report them to the dean?

73
00:05:37,522 --> 00:05:39,602
No need.

74
00:05:39,602 --> 00:05:41,270
So, you'll just let them?

75
00:05:41,270 --> 00:05:43,038
It's not that I'll just let them be,

76
00:05:43,038 --> 00:05:46,575
but I just thought Lina will be blamed

77
00:05:46,575 --> 00:05:50,012
because she's the one
who called me to go there.

78
00:05:50,012 --> 00:05:54,817
That's how Camille and Aira
work by deniability.

79
00:05:54,817 --> 00:05:57,609
I'm sure if I'll report them,
they'll just deny it.

80
00:05:57,609 --> 00:06:01,318
And in the end,
Lina will be the one reprimanded by the dean.

81
00:06:01,318 --> 00:06:04,527
She might even get suspended
even if in truth,

82
00:06:04,527 --> 00:06:08,664
she was just being used in this situation.

83
00:06:08,664 --> 00:06:12,667
She's a victim...
A victim of Camille and Aira just like me.

84
00:06:17,371 --> 00:06:20,776
But still, she let them use her.

85
00:06:20,776 --> 00:06:24,082
Nero, not everyone is as brave as you.

86
00:06:24,082 --> 00:06:27,484
And not everyone can make a stand easily.

87
00:06:29,616 --> 00:06:33,553
If you'll let this slide now,
for sure, they'll just repeat it.

88
00:06:37,993 --> 00:06:41,263
Don't worry, I'll just be careful.

89
00:06:41,263 --> 00:06:43,832
Extra, extra, more.

90
00:06:45,998 --> 00:06:48,166
Just forget about that.

91
00:06:56,212 --> 00:06:58,947
You're really a good person, Florence.

92
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:04,117
I told you, you're not difficult to like.

93
00:07:26,408 --> 00:07:27,876
I'll go to my class.

94
00:07:27,876 --> 00:07:29,395
Me too.

95
00:07:35,272 --> 00:07:37,140
Where are you going?

96
00:07:40,995 --> 00:07:42,963
To the classroom.

97
00:08:04,623 --> 00:08:07,158
You're really a good person, Florence.

98
00:08:07,994 --> 00:08:12,431
I told you, you're not difficult to like.

99
00:08:15,357 --> 00:08:17,192
Go to sleep, Florence.

100
00:08:17,192 --> 00:08:19,160
Go to sleep.

101
00:08:51,860 --> 00:08:55,264
My name is Ashley Salongga
but you can call me Ash.

102
00:08:55,264 --> 00:08:57,199
And welcome to GU TV.

103
00:08:57,199 --> 00:09:00,969
This is the official streaming channel
of Gyronella University.

104
00:09:00,969 --> 00:09:03,205
So whoever you are, our dear hearts,

105
00:09:03,205 --> 00:09:07,576
fellow family members, siblings,
chatter, or whatever you may be.

106
00:09:07,576 --> 00:09:12,014
This is your go to place
for anything and everything Gyronellan.

107
00:09:12,014 --> 00:09:14,216
And for our pilot episode,

108
00:09:14,216 --> 00:09:18,420
we'll talk about a very important
and special day

109
00:09:18,420 --> 00:09:20,522
that is unique for Gyronella University.

110
00:09:20,522 --> 00:09:24,026
A day we like to call Agora Day.

111
00:09:24,026 --> 00:09:26,095
But what is Agora Day?

112
00:09:26,095 --> 00:09:31,205
Why is this so important for the Gyronellans?

113
00:09:31,205 --> 00:09:34,803
What's this? Is this a party?

114
00:09:34,803 --> 00:09:37,841
Is this the same level as Coachella?

115
00:09:37,841 --> 00:09:43,379
Why does GU have something called Agora Day?

116
00:09:43,379 --> 00:09:45,822
And to discuss more about that,

117
00:09:45,822 --> 00:09:50,119
I invited a special someone
today with us here in the studio.

118
00:09:50,119 --> 00:09:56,058
He is one of the brightest
and smartest students of our university,

119
00:09:56,058 --> 00:09:57,416
and not to mention,

120
00:09:57,416 --> 00:10:00,629
he will be the next leader
of our third-world country.

121
00:10:00,629 --> 00:10:06,034
Please welcome to the studio,
none other than Sean Owen Ferell.

122
00:10:09,838 --> 00:10:12,040
Welcome to our first broadcast, Owen.

123
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:14,143
So glad to have you here.

124
00:10:14,143 --> 00:10:17,980
Well, it seems I have no choice
after you blackmailed me

125
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:19,948
to be a part of this program.

126
00:10:19,948 --> 00:10:21,083
Exactly.

127
00:10:21,083 --> 00:10:24,953
So, let's head on to our first question.

128
00:10:27,156 --> 00:10:29,023
Are you still single?

129
00:10:31,069 --> 00:10:32,795
It's just a joke. Just joking.

130
00:10:32,795 --> 00:10:34,907
It's just to get the ball rolling.

131
00:10:34,907 --> 00:10:37,733
But... Okay, here it is.

132
00:10:37,733 --> 00:10:40,369
You are here to talk about Agora Day.

133
00:10:40,369 --> 00:10:44,406
So, please tell me and our viewers

134
00:10:44,406 --> 00:10:46,574
what this day is all about.

135
00:10:47,476 --> 00:10:49,578
Well it's not a party, Ash.

136
00:10:49,578 --> 00:10:54,562
But maybe the correct definition
is it's a celebration.

137
00:10:54,562 --> 00:10:57,064
A celebration of democracy.

138
00:10:58,120 --> 00:11:00,875
Wow, democracy.

139
00:11:00,875 --> 00:11:02,858
Big word.

140
00:11:02,858 --> 00:11:04,497
Exactly.

141
00:11:04,497 --> 00:11:06,795
Because today is the day we Gyronellans

142
00:11:06,795 --> 00:11:09,565
will be able to nominate
our student representatives.

143
00:11:09,565 --> 00:11:11,513
Each department of the university

144
00:11:11,513 --> 00:11:14,236
has the chance
to elect its student representative.

145
00:11:14,236 --> 00:11:16,505
The reason why we call this Agora Day

146
00:11:16,505 --> 00:11:20,784
is that we're trying to mimic
the Greek concept of Agora Market,

147
00:11:20,784 --> 00:11:23,812
the earliest form of democracy.

148
00:11:23,812 --> 00:11:28,050
Where the stakeholders
will gather whatever their background is

149
00:11:28,050 --> 00:11:30,283
to vote for their student leaders.

150
00:11:30,283 --> 00:11:33,190
So how are the elections done?

151
00:11:33,190 --> 00:11:35,090
Well, it's just simple.

152
00:11:35,090 --> 00:11:38,560
The student will nominate
the most popular from the department.

153
00:11:38,560 --> 00:11:40,267
Starting with Economics,

154
00:11:40,267 --> 00:11:43,733
Philosophy, Business Management, Marketing,

155
00:11:43,734 --> 00:11:46,004
and of course, Communication Arts.

156
00:11:46,004 --> 00:11:49,267
And if no one will comment or challenge them,

157
00:11:49,267 --> 00:11:52,975
then he or she will automatically become
the student representative.

158
00:11:52,975 --> 00:11:58,680
Oh, but what happens
if someone makes a challenge?

159
00:11:59,748 --> 00:12:02,967
That has never happened in the history of GU.

160
00:12:02,968 --> 00:12:06,889
All the time, students vote
for the most popular, and influential,

161
00:12:06,889 --> 00:12:09,725
especially if they come
from an influential family.

162
00:12:09,725 --> 00:12:12,460
<i>So no one will bother to challenge them.</i>

163
00:12:14,730 --> 00:12:17,299
It's tiring.

164
00:12:17,299 --> 00:12:19,434
I wonder where are those three fools?

165
00:12:19,434 --> 00:12:20,983
Yeah, it's pretty.

166
00:12:22,037 --> 00:12:25,307
I love the assorted ones.

167
00:12:25,307 --> 00:12:27,901
It's so fab.

168
00:12:27,901 --> 00:12:30,585
Oh, yeah. I love red as well.

169
00:12:31,613 --> 00:12:32,915
Speaking of the devil.

170
00:12:32,915 --> 00:12:36,852
It's a cutie... the sunflowers.

171
00:12:36,852 --> 00:12:39,121
Yes, it's a cutie.

172
00:12:39,121 --> 00:12:40,988
Bro.

173
00:12:42,457 --> 00:12:43,859
It's weirdo, I mean, Nero.

174
00:12:43,859 --> 00:12:47,396
- Sorry, it sounds alike.
- The half has a different nationality.

175
00:12:47,396 --> 00:12:48,830
Where are you going?

176
00:12:48,830 --> 00:12:50,070
Hello.

177
00:12:50,070 --> 00:12:52,298
Hello, everybody.

178
00:12:52,298 --> 00:12:56,672
Hello, Gyronellans,
and welcome to our Agora Day.

179
00:12:56,672 --> 00:12:58,949
Today is a very important day

180
00:12:58,949 --> 00:13:01,610
because we will be deciding
who from the student committee

181
00:13:01,610 --> 00:13:06,915
will be working with me
in organizing our exciting activities.

182
00:13:06,915 --> 00:13:11,734
So, are you ready
to elect our representatives?

183
00:13:11,734 --> 00:13:13,762
Yeah!

184
00:13:22,798 --> 00:13:25,953
Let us start with Philosophy.

185
00:13:27,734 --> 00:13:29,671
We nominate Socrates,

186
00:13:29,671 --> 00:13:33,841
the greatest thinker of all the universe.

187
00:13:37,846 --> 00:13:42,618
You can't nominate someone who is...
well, dead.

188
00:13:42,618 --> 00:13:44,819
Socrates will never die.

189
00:13:44,819 --> 00:13:48,161
He will continue to live
in our hearts and minds.

190
00:13:48,161 --> 00:13:53,248
His thoughts and ideas are
the foundation of our civilization.

191
00:13:53,248 --> 00:13:58,404
So, he is alive
because he lives within all of us.

192
00:13:58,404 --> 00:14:00,572
What about Marketing?

193
00:14:02,938 --> 00:14:05,907
We nominate Lester Sumalangit.

194
00:14:06,919 --> 00:14:09,187
Any objections?

195
00:14:13,222 --> 00:14:16,725
Anyone who'd like to challenge
this nomination?

196
00:14:21,356 --> 00:14:26,327
Alright, then that makes Lester
the head of the Marketing department.

197
00:14:35,451 --> 00:14:37,239
Economics?

198
00:14:37,239 --> 00:14:41,409
We nominate Margaret Reyes
for the economics department.

199
00:14:42,639 --> 00:14:44,874
Any objections?

200
00:14:47,020 --> 00:14:51,858
Well, then that makes Margaret
the head of the Economics department.

201
00:14:59,628 --> 00:15:02,464
How about Business Management?

202
00:15:02,464 --> 00:15:06,334
We nominate Tristan Mateo Ferell.

203
00:15:08,648 --> 00:15:10,883
Any objections?

204
00:15:12,345 --> 00:15:14,442
Any challenges?

205
00:15:15,579 --> 00:15:17,659
Alright, then that makes Tristan

206
00:15:17,659 --> 00:15:20,748
the head of
the Business Management department.

207
00:15:25,679 --> 00:15:28,790
Finally, let's move on to Com Arts.

208
00:15:28,790 --> 00:15:32,527
Who will be the head of
the Com arts Department?

209
00:15:33,875 --> 00:15:37,277
We nominate Camille Cortez Villarico.

210
00:15:39,068 --> 00:15:41,236
Any objections?

211
00:15:46,408 --> 00:15:49,810
Anyone that would like
to challenge this nomination?

212
00:15:54,827 --> 00:15:57,552
Alright, then that makes
Camille the head of the...

213
00:15:57,552 --> 00:15:59,487
I object!

214
00:16:00,856 --> 00:16:02,983
She objects.

215
00:16:13,435 --> 00:16:16,037
I challenge her nomination...

216
00:16:16,805 --> 00:16:21,397
and I nominate myself
to be the student representative

217
00:16:21,397 --> 00:16:24,299
of the Communication Arts department.

218
00:16:39,494 --> 00:16:41,196
That's possible, right?

219
00:16:41,196 --> 00:16:45,801
I can challenge her nomination
and nominate myself.

220
00:16:45,801 --> 00:16:47,616
Definitely.

221
00:16:47,616 --> 00:16:51,505
We were just shocked
because this is something new.

222
00:16:52,319 --> 00:16:54,718
Excuse me?

223
00:16:54,718 --> 00:16:56,911
How dare you!

224
00:16:58,507 --> 00:17:02,651
Well as the rules suggest,
if we have two nominees,

225
00:17:02,651 --> 00:17:05,453
both will be given a chance
to convince you to choose them

226
00:17:05,453 --> 00:17:07,389
as your representative.

227
00:17:07,389 --> 00:17:11,359
We will reconvene to decide
who, between Camille and Florence,

228
00:17:11,359 --> 00:17:13,470
will the student body choose

229
00:17:13,470 --> 00:17:16,597
to be the representative
of the Communication Arts department.

230
00:17:21,436 --> 00:17:23,544
This is a complete shock!

231
00:17:23,544 --> 00:17:26,341
For the first time ever
in the university's history,

232
00:17:26,341 --> 00:17:28,714
there are two nominees for the representative

233
00:17:28,714 --> 00:17:31,224
of the Communication Arts department.

234
00:17:31,224 --> 00:17:35,121
And to give us additional insight
on this historical event,

235
00:17:35,121 --> 00:17:39,325
let's welcome to the studio,
Aldus Rafael Ferell.

236
00:17:39,325 --> 00:17:43,730
You're right, this is new territory
for our beloved university.

237
00:17:43,730 --> 00:17:46,480
And you see, we have a tradition here.

238
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:51,637
The richest student, the most influential,
and the biggest clout

239
00:17:51,637 --> 00:17:56,032
is automatically elected as representative
of their respective departments.

240
00:17:56,032 --> 00:17:58,985
And all the time, no one objects.

241
00:17:58,985 --> 00:18:01,547
You know, when Camille topped
the dean's list last year,

242
00:18:01,547 --> 00:18:05,751
everyone expected her to become
the representative of Com Arts.

243
00:18:05,751 --> 00:18:09,541
And to add to that,
she's the most popular in her batch.

244
00:18:09,541 --> 00:18:11,933
So she's a shoo-in already
as the departmental rep.

245
00:18:11,934 --> 00:18:12,734
Tradition dictates

246
00:18:12,734 --> 00:18:17,166
that she should sit
on the highest throne of Com Arts.

247
00:18:17,167 --> 00:18:19,500
But for the first time in history,

248
00:18:19,501 --> 00:18:23,235
someone is willing
to go against that tradition.

249
00:18:23,235 --> 00:18:26,999
And for a school
that governs strong traditions,

250
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:30,239
this Florence girl is way over her head.

251
00:18:30,239 --> 00:18:32,500
You may ask why?

252
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:33,843
She's a freshman.

253
00:18:33,843 --> 00:18:36,820
We don't even know
what's her family background.

254
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:39,549
Well, I heard
that she's one of the beneficiaries

255
00:18:39,549 --> 00:18:41,666
of our school's Scholarship Program.

256
00:18:41,667 --> 00:18:42,785
That's good for her.

257
00:18:42,785 --> 00:18:46,389
I heard that she cooks well...

258
00:18:46,389 --> 00:18:50,891
but does she have the capabilities
to become a representative of Com Arts?

259
00:18:50,891 --> 00:18:54,130
Well, either way,
we cannot independently verify the claim

260
00:18:54,130 --> 00:18:56,098
that she's a good cook.

261
00:18:59,168 --> 00:19:02,219
So, what will happen now?

262
00:19:02,219 --> 00:19:04,240
Well, we could do what the Greeks did

263
00:19:04,240 --> 00:19:08,510
before they were trivialized
by Zack Snyder in the movie "300".

264
00:19:09,645 --> 00:19:13,549
I mean, anyway,
we can solve this by casting our votes.

265
00:19:13,549 --> 00:19:17,053
According to the rules,
there's no unanimous decision,

266
00:19:17,053 --> 00:19:21,490
and every student will be given
a chance to vote.

267
00:19:22,892 --> 00:19:24,660
And each candidate, in this case,

268
00:19:24,660 --> 00:19:27,764
Camille and Florence have a chance

269
00:19:27,764 --> 00:19:30,933
to introduce themselves
to the whole student body.

270
00:19:32,368 --> 00:19:35,582
So, what do you think, Aldus?

271
00:19:35,582 --> 00:19:37,440
Who are you rooting for in this battle?

272
00:19:37,440 --> 00:19:39,642
Well, it's...

273
00:19:39,642 --> 00:19:42,010
I will answer that question.

274
00:19:44,465 --> 00:19:48,155
<i>The odds are definitely against Florence.</i>

275
00:19:48,155 --> 00:19:52,426
<i>I will shave my head
if she will win over Camille.</i>

276
00:19:52,426 --> 00:19:56,840
<i>I mean, we love David vs Goliath stories,</i>

277
00:19:56,840 --> 00:19:59,575
<i>but David is an exemption.</i>

278
00:19:59,575 --> 00:20:03,496
Because in reality, Goliath always wins.

279
00:20:03,496 --> 00:20:05,473
You can even ask the USA Dream Team

280
00:20:05,473 --> 00:20:08,570
or the National Football Team of Germany.

281
00:20:11,374 --> 00:20:14,594
I have nothing against you, Florence.

282
00:20:14,594 --> 00:20:16,379
But the truth is,

283
00:20:16,379 --> 00:20:18,881
<i>you have no chance of winning.</i>

284
00:20:18,881 --> 00:20:20,477
<i>Period!</i>

285
00:20:29,031 --> 00:20:32,795
What came into your mind, Florencia?

286
00:20:32,795 --> 00:20:35,430
Why did you nominate yourself?

287
00:20:39,769 --> 00:20:42,872
Don't tell me you're having second thoughts.

288
00:20:42,872 --> 00:20:45,745
Me, having second thoughts?

289
00:20:45,745 --> 00:20:47,487
Of course not. Me, of all people.

290
00:20:47,487 --> 00:20:49,322
Of course not.

291
00:20:57,220 --> 00:21:02,168
Yes, I don't know why I nominated myself.

292
00:21:02,168 --> 00:21:05,628
I don't know what went into my mind earlier.

293
00:21:05,628 --> 00:21:08,363
It's because you followed your heart.

294
00:21:09,198 --> 00:21:11,238
In the short time that you're here,

295
00:21:11,238 --> 00:21:15,500
you found out what kind of person Camille
and her friends are.

296
00:21:15,500 --> 00:21:18,107
And you felt like you had to do something.

297
00:21:18,107 --> 00:21:19,880
Your heart is telling you

298
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:23,915
that you can't let them take the position
just to terrorize others.

299
00:21:23,915 --> 00:21:26,415
And even if you're not thinking about it,

300
00:21:26,415 --> 00:21:28,784
you followed your heart.

301
00:21:32,392 --> 00:21:37,343
But my heart is putting me in danger.

302
00:21:37,343 --> 00:21:40,453
Why, did your heart ever put you in danger?

303
00:21:43,766 --> 00:21:47,732
You know, with the short time I've known you,

304
00:21:47,732 --> 00:21:49,771
your best quality...

305
00:21:52,755 --> 00:21:54,590
is your heart.

306
00:21:55,611 --> 00:21:59,615
There are a lot of intelligent
and witty people in this world.

307
00:21:59,615 --> 00:22:03,019
But if there are more people like you,

308
00:22:03,019 --> 00:22:04,587
this world would be so different.

309
00:22:04,587 --> 00:22:06,690
It will be a whole lot better.

310
00:22:06,690 --> 00:22:09,250
So don't doubt yourself.

311
00:22:09,250 --> 00:22:13,153
Show everybody the power of your heart.

312
00:22:28,277 --> 00:22:30,614
She has the nerve!

313
00:22:30,614 --> 00:22:35,630
She's really something
to challenge me out in the open.

314
00:22:35,630 --> 00:22:37,153
I hate her.

315
00:22:37,153 --> 00:22:41,357
Every fiber of my being hates her.

316
00:22:41,357 --> 00:22:44,560
Relax, you're overreacting.

317
00:22:44,560 --> 00:22:46,862
"Relax, you're overreacting".

318
00:22:46,862 --> 00:22:50,723
If she did this to you,
for sure you'll overreact too.

319
00:22:50,723 --> 00:22:53,336
Don't vent your frustrations on me.

320
00:22:53,336 --> 00:22:55,670
We're on the same side here.

321
00:22:56,772 --> 00:22:58,274
You're right.

322
00:22:58,274 --> 00:23:00,512
I'm sorry.

323
00:23:00,512 --> 00:23:03,047
I just really hate her.

324
00:23:04,680 --> 00:23:07,917
Did I already say
that every fiber of my being hates her?

325
00:23:07,917 --> 00:23:10,920
Yes, you've been saying that line
over and over.

326
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:14,257
And that's a symptom
that she's getting into you.

327
00:23:14,257 --> 00:23:18,317
So just calm down because you'll still win.

328
00:23:18,317 --> 00:23:19,891
I know.

329
00:23:20,930 --> 00:23:23,099
I can't just believe that she has the audacity....

330
00:23:23,099 --> 00:23:25,801
to challenge me out in the open.

331
00:23:25,801 --> 00:23:29,260
Don't worry, you'll have a chance.

332
00:23:30,229 --> 00:23:32,079
A chance for what?

333
00:23:32,079 --> 00:23:36,838
A chance for us to destroy her
once and for all.

334
00:23:36,838 --> 00:23:38,245
How?

335
00:23:40,116 --> 00:23:42,526
Here is Michael.

336
00:23:43,385 --> 00:23:45,463
What can he do?

337
00:23:45,463 --> 00:23:48,457
Well, I can do anything, Camille.

338
00:23:48,457 --> 00:23:51,531
I can do a new reality.

339
00:23:51,531 --> 00:23:55,738
As they say, perception is real,

340
00:23:55,738 --> 00:23:57,266
truth is not.

341
00:23:57,266 --> 00:23:58,868
Exactly.

342
00:23:58,868 --> 00:24:00,670
Michael can do anything.

343
00:24:00,670 --> 00:24:03,677
He is the best graphic artist
in the university,

344
00:24:03,677 --> 00:24:07,084
and he will help us create one story
that is so humiliating,

345
00:24:07,084 --> 00:24:10,546
Florence will have no choice
but to quit school.

346
00:24:10,546 --> 00:24:15,427
In the great tradition of disinformation.

347
00:24:18,454 --> 00:24:20,012
Great job.

348
00:24:22,491 --> 00:24:24,384
Florence is really a fool.

349
00:24:24,384 --> 00:24:26,831
Because of her, our Agora day is extended.

350
00:24:26,831 --> 00:24:30,301
You know, we should be supporting her.

351
00:24:30,301 --> 00:24:33,237
I'm not saying we will not support her,

352
00:24:33,237 --> 00:24:37,108
but does she have a realistic chance
against Camille?

353
00:24:37,108 --> 00:24:40,144
Of course not, but it's not about winning.

354
00:24:40,144 --> 00:24:42,346
At this point, you already know Florence.

355
00:24:42,346 --> 00:24:44,582
It's more about making a point.

356
00:24:44,582 --> 00:24:46,551
Exactly.

357
00:24:46,551 --> 00:24:48,352
Do you know where Owen is?

358
00:24:48,352 --> 00:24:49,754
Owen?

359
00:24:49,754 --> 00:24:52,723
Maybe he's campaigning for Florence.

360
00:24:52,723 --> 00:24:55,159
Among the four of us,
he's the one who supports Florence.

361
00:24:55,159 --> 00:24:56,427
I told you so.

362
00:24:56,427 --> 00:24:58,896
I think to some degree,

363
00:24:58,896 --> 00:25:01,032
he and Florence are very much alike.

364
00:25:01,032 --> 00:25:04,068
I mean, they think the same way.

365
00:25:04,068 --> 00:25:06,859
They believe in something
that is difficult to believe.

366
00:25:08,039 --> 00:25:10,093
You can say that again.

367
00:25:16,700 --> 00:25:21,319
With what we're about to do,
that girl will stand no chance.

368
00:25:21,319 --> 00:25:22,854
We will ruin her.

369
00:25:22,854 --> 00:25:24,934
We will destroy her.

370
00:25:26,005 --> 00:25:28,926
Let's destroy Florence.

371
00:25:28,926 --> 00:25:33,716
Get rid of her irritating existence.

372
00:25:43,808 --> 00:25:48,379
I know you're all excited
because today we're a new territory.

373
00:25:48,379 --> 00:25:52,750
And I know that I've been hearing
that these shouldn't be happening,

374
00:25:52,750 --> 00:25:55,314
that there are traditions in Agora.

375
00:25:55,314 --> 00:25:59,681
However, just like any tradition,

376
00:25:59,681 --> 00:26:03,261
this is subject to gradual change.

377
00:26:03,261 --> 00:26:07,365
And today, we will figure out
if this tradition is good.

378
00:26:07,365 --> 00:26:09,142
And at the same time,

379
00:26:09,142 --> 00:26:13,838
we will decide who will be the representative
of the Com Arts department.

380
00:26:13,838 --> 00:26:18,135
I now present to you, Camille and Florence.

381
00:26:25,877 --> 00:26:28,234
I will destroy you.

382
00:26:34,959 --> 00:26:36,860
Now is your chance, Florence,

383
00:26:36,860 --> 00:26:43,462
to introduce yourself and convince them
that you deserve the position.

384
00:26:45,303 --> 00:26:47,408
Thank you, Antonia.

385
00:26:53,843 --> 00:26:55,812
Hello.

386
00:26:57,214 --> 00:27:04,722
I'm sure you're now thinking
that I'm thick-skinned,

387
00:27:04,722 --> 00:27:12,123
because I'm going against
the flow of your trend in Agora

388
00:27:12,123 --> 00:27:17,068
and your tradition too.

389
00:27:17,068 --> 00:27:19,470
Who the hell are you?

390
00:27:21,900 --> 00:27:25,476
I'm Florence Dela Cruz.

391
00:27:25,476 --> 00:27:27,931
You should not be here.

392
00:27:35,987 --> 00:27:38,289
You're right.

393
00:27:38,289 --> 00:27:40,891
I should not be here.

394
00:27:40,891 --> 00:27:43,928
But there's nothing you can do

395
00:27:43,928 --> 00:27:48,187
because I'm now here in front of you.

396
00:27:50,001 --> 00:27:58,042
The truth is, I don't know why I did this...

397
00:27:59,176 --> 00:28:08,753
but someone told me
that's because I'm following my heart.

398
00:28:10,121 --> 00:28:15,043
So, here I am, following my heart,

399
00:28:15,043 --> 00:28:23,501
and I know it's corny,
or using your term, cringe.

400
00:28:24,902 --> 00:28:29,006
Even though I've been here in GU
for only a couple of days,

401
00:28:29,006 --> 00:28:31,861
I can see the real you.

402
00:28:34,979 --> 00:28:37,137
Oh my gosh.

403
00:28:38,015 --> 00:28:39,884
- Yes.
- Girl!

404
00:28:39,884 --> 00:28:41,252
- <i>My heart sees you.</i>
- Hurry up!

405
00:28:41,252 --> 00:28:42,334
Stop limping around.

406
00:28:42,334 --> 00:28:45,282
<i>And my heart can hear you too.</i>

407
00:28:45,282 --> 00:28:48,059
<i>That's why I can feel
what you're going through here.</i>

408
00:28:48,059 --> 00:28:50,268
Hey! Zoom in on her.

409
00:28:52,763 --> 00:29:01,246
And sometimes what I can see,
hear, and feel...

410
00:29:01,246 --> 00:29:04,205
can crush the heart.

411
00:29:05,543 --> 00:29:08,171
Which is ironic.

412
00:29:08,171 --> 00:29:09,716
Because, with our time now,

413
00:29:09,716 --> 00:29:14,263
<i>there are a lot of devices and ways
to put ourselves out there,</i>

414
00:29:14,263 --> 00:29:22,927
<i>but it seems no one sees,
hears, or feels each one of us.</i>

415
00:29:25,196 --> 00:29:31,770
Every day we save our courage
to step out of our safe spaces

416
00:29:31,770 --> 00:29:34,609
and offer ourselves to the world.

417
00:29:36,062 --> 00:29:42,079
But I can sense that you are scared.

418
00:29:42,079 --> 00:29:45,113
You are scared to be yourselves.

419
00:29:45,983 --> 00:29:54,715
We are scared to be judged
and to commit mistakes.

420
00:29:55,582 --> 00:30:00,860
That's why, here I am
standing in front of you to say

421
00:30:00,860 --> 00:30:06,195
I can see, feel, and hear you all.

422
00:30:07,233 --> 00:30:10,775
I understand all of you.

423
00:30:10,775 --> 00:30:13,444
We all want the same thing.

424
00:30:13,444 --> 00:30:18,989
We have the same fears and worries,

425
00:30:18,989 --> 00:30:23,826
and we all want
to be the best versions of ourselves.

426
00:30:25,656 --> 00:30:31,896
So, what I'm trying to say is...

427
00:30:31,896 --> 00:30:36,061
I am here in front of you, offering myself.

428
00:30:37,608 --> 00:30:40,104
I don't have much.

429
00:30:40,104 --> 00:30:46,143
I don't really have much to offer.

430
00:30:46,143 --> 00:30:50,114
But if you need a person to listen,

431
00:30:50,114 --> 00:30:53,450
if you need someone to talk to,

432
00:30:53,450 --> 00:30:58,956
to understand what you're going through,

433
00:30:58,956 --> 00:31:01,498
and that the very least...

434
00:31:03,178 --> 00:31:05,996
I can be that person.

435
00:31:05,996 --> 00:31:11,293
And I promise, I will never judge you.

436
00:31:13,537 --> 00:31:14,805
That's all.

437
00:31:14,805 --> 00:31:19,817
Thank you for giving me
a chance to talk to you.

438
00:32:00,302 --> 00:32:03,564
Blah, blah, blah.

439
00:32:12,396 --> 00:32:15,299
That was a nice speech.

440
00:32:15,299 --> 00:32:20,938
"I see you, I hear you, I feel you."

441
00:32:20,938 --> 00:32:26,043
And she validates each one of you.

442
00:32:26,043 --> 00:32:29,793
As if all feelings are valid.

443
00:32:29,793 --> 00:32:32,783
So blah, blah, blah.

444
00:32:32,783 --> 00:32:34,339
Again.

445
00:32:37,154 --> 00:32:42,562
Well, let me tell you this,
how about my feelings?

446
00:32:43,460 --> 00:32:45,726
Aren't my feelings valid?

447
00:32:47,047 --> 00:32:49,533
I am the victim here.

448
00:32:49,533 --> 00:32:53,537
Tradition dictates
that I should be the Com Arts representative.

449
00:32:53,537 --> 00:32:59,310
I am the top of my class,
of our batch to be exact.

450
00:32:59,310 --> 00:33:01,946
I am the one you all know.

451
00:33:01,946 --> 00:33:05,162
I'm the face of my department.

452
00:33:05,162 --> 00:33:08,118
Not to mention, my dad recently made it

453
00:33:08,118 --> 00:33:11,654
to Forbes Magazine Billionaire's List.

454
00:33:15,810 --> 00:33:19,596
That is why I should be
your Com Arts representative.

455
00:33:19,596 --> 00:33:23,968
Because at the very least,
that's what is due to me.

456
00:33:23,968 --> 00:33:25,836
That's what it should be.

457
00:33:25,836 --> 00:33:28,272
I'm entitled to it.

458
00:33:28,272 --> 00:33:30,376
But okay,

459
00:33:30,376 --> 00:33:33,050
let's just assume...

460
00:33:33,050 --> 00:33:38,983
let's just say
that tradition does not matter.

461
00:33:38,983 --> 00:33:44,228
Let's not do anymore
what we are used to doing.

462
00:33:46,290 --> 00:33:49,827
Judge us for who we are.

463
00:33:49,827 --> 00:33:51,729
Game.

464
00:33:51,729 --> 00:33:53,620
Do you think

465
00:33:53,620 --> 00:33:56,916
she is worthy
to be your Com Arts representative?

466
00:33:56,916 --> 00:33:58,532
Bea?

467
00:34:17,254 --> 00:34:18,988
Michelle?

468
00:34:30,134 --> 00:34:31,535
Ooh...

469
00:34:31,535 --> 00:34:33,049
Next.

470
00:34:37,374 --> 00:34:38,975
Next.

471
00:34:41,957 --> 00:34:43,506
Next.

472
00:34:46,583 --> 00:34:50,053
Camille, that's not true.

473
00:34:52,389 --> 00:34:57,494
Girl, this is my time,
so please don't interrupt me.

474
00:34:57,494 --> 00:34:59,795
Don't be rude.

475
00:35:03,500 --> 00:35:06,709
I agree guys, she's pretty charming.

476
00:35:06,709 --> 00:35:10,174
I, for a fact, wanted to be her friend too.

477
00:35:10,174 --> 00:35:13,386
But yesterday, I saw her.

478
00:35:14,244 --> 00:35:17,011
I saw her making a fool of herself.

479
00:35:18,248 --> 00:35:22,292
That's why I took those photos
because my eyes couldn't believe it.

480
00:35:23,604 --> 00:35:30,254
So, is that the representative that you want?

481
00:35:31,562 --> 00:35:33,931
Someone who is so messed up.

482
00:35:33,931 --> 00:35:39,570
Oh my, she might mess up something
in the student body.

483
00:35:39,570 --> 00:35:43,868
So, if you guys still don't believe
that I should be the Com Arts representative,

484
00:35:43,868 --> 00:35:45,600
don't let the face

485
00:35:45,601 --> 00:35:50,680
of one of the most dynamic departments
of this university

486
00:35:50,680 --> 00:35:54,212
be someone with questionable morals.

487
00:35:55,319 --> 00:35:59,156
She doesn't deserve
to be your representative.

488
00:35:59,156 --> 00:36:02,155
She doesn't even deserve
to be in this school.

489
00:36:10,434 --> 00:36:12,285
That's enough.

490
00:36:15,706 --> 00:36:18,842
It's impossible that you saw her yesterday...

491
00:36:18,842 --> 00:36:20,621
that's why that's not true.

492
00:36:22,012 --> 00:36:24,223
What makes you say that?

493
00:36:29,786 --> 00:36:34,235
Because we were together yesterday.

494
00:36:45,502 --> 00:36:47,070
Why are you together?

495
00:36:47,070 --> 00:36:48,829
Do you even know her?

496
00:36:55,337 --> 00:36:56,581
She's my girlfriend.

497
00:36:56,581 --> 00:36:58,407
Oh my God!

498
00:37:05,088 --> 00:37:07,640
That's why what you're saying is impossible,

499
00:37:07,640 --> 00:37:09,858
because we were together yesterday.

500
00:37:13,929 --> 00:37:16,065
You're kidding, right?

501
00:37:16,065 --> 00:37:19,735
So, you're saying you know this woman,

502
00:37:19,735 --> 00:37:22,459
and you're in a relationship?

503
00:37:25,141 --> 00:37:27,593
Nero is saying that you're lying.

504
00:37:29,678 --> 00:37:32,948
And now I'm the liar?

505
00:37:32,948 --> 00:37:36,699
So, are you saying the Ferells are liars?

506
00:37:37,753 --> 00:37:40,723
And maybe you want
to check the Forbes list that you're saying.

507
00:37:40,723 --> 00:37:44,660
Check what place are we
on the list of billionaires.

508
00:37:44,660 --> 00:37:46,583
And not to mention,

509
00:37:46,583 --> 00:37:50,833
accusing us of lying is something
our family won't let you get away with it.

510
00:37:50,833 --> 00:37:53,448
Because the Ferells are many things.

511
00:37:53,448 --> 00:37:55,738
But to lie?

512
00:37:55,738 --> 00:37:57,673
We can't do that.

513
00:37:57,673 --> 00:38:01,268
You know, that's enough.

514
00:38:01,268 --> 00:38:03,451
Let's proceed to vote.

515
00:39:49,852 --> 00:39:51,634
Camille, stop!

516
00:39:51,634 --> 00:39:53,589
I hate her!

517
00:39:53,589 --> 00:39:55,557
Why is she doing this to me?

518
00:39:55,557 --> 00:39:58,861
Why is this happening?

519
00:39:58,861 --> 00:40:00,793
What are you looking at?

520
00:40:06,502 --> 00:40:09,442
Ms. Villarico, can I talk to you?

521
00:40:12,007 --> 00:40:13,482
Dean?

522
00:40:24,720 --> 00:40:26,889
Girlfriend? I'm your girlfriend, Nero?

523
00:40:26,889 --> 00:40:28,057
Since when?

524
00:40:28,057 --> 00:40:31,126
I wasn't informed
and I didn't even receive a memo.

525
00:40:31,126 --> 00:40:32,728
Don't you want it?

526
00:40:32,728 --> 00:40:35,364
What do you mean "Don't I want it"?

527
00:40:35,364 --> 00:40:38,534
To be fair, Nero has a point.

528
00:40:38,534 --> 00:40:41,470
It's a privilege
to be a girlfriend of a Ferell.

529
00:40:41,470 --> 00:40:42,671
Stop it.

530
00:40:42,671 --> 00:40:46,175
And you too,
is it true that the Ferells never lie?

531
00:40:46,175 --> 00:40:49,778
So, what do you call what Nero did earlier?
It's the truth?

532
00:40:49,778 --> 00:40:51,280
I know we live in a post-truth world

533
00:40:51,280 --> 00:40:54,590
but that's not a license for all of us to lie.

534
00:40:55,451 --> 00:40:57,586
Well, technically, that's not a lie.

535
00:40:57,586 --> 00:41:01,457
What technically are you talking about?

536
00:41:01,457 --> 00:41:05,594
Technically,
you were in the mansion last night.

537
00:41:05,594 --> 00:41:11,400
You were with me, Troy, Aldus, Tristan,

538
00:41:11,400 --> 00:41:15,535
Grandfather Garp, Ma'am Serafica...

539
00:41:15,535 --> 00:41:17,093
and Nero.

540
00:41:19,641 --> 00:41:22,644
I was in the mansion last night
because I'm your cook.

541
00:41:22,644 --> 00:41:26,960
Exactly, so Nero is not lying.

542
00:41:29,318 --> 00:41:31,653
What are you talking about?

543
00:41:31,653 --> 00:41:34,556
He told the whole school
that I'm his girlfriend.

544
00:41:34,556 --> 00:41:36,325
And I'm not his girlfriend, I'm your cook.

545
00:41:36,325 --> 00:41:38,612
Isn't that a lie?

546
00:41:42,264 --> 00:41:43,665
Are you happy?

547
00:41:43,665 --> 00:41:46,132
Yes, very happy.

548
00:41:46,133 --> 00:41:49,176
Are you happy that you're Nero's girlfriend?

549
00:41:55,277 --> 00:41:56,412
What's this?

550
00:41:56,412 --> 00:41:59,020
Dream within a dream?

551
00:41:59,020 --> 00:42:01,049
Wake up, Florence. Wake up.

552
00:42:01,049 --> 00:42:02,885
Why are you hurting yourself?

553
00:42:02,885 --> 00:42:04,319
You are not real.

554
00:42:04,319 --> 00:42:06,595
I won't be flirting with you

555
00:42:06,595 --> 00:42:09,028
because I'm a good, good, girl
in a good, good, world

556
00:42:09,028 --> 00:42:11,375
and it's not good thing if you kiss me.

557
00:42:11,375 --> 00:42:13,233
What do you need?

558
00:42:13,234 --> 00:42:15,336
She's a good person.

559
00:42:15,336 --> 00:42:17,142
Don't hurt her.

560
00:42:17,142 --> 00:42:19,540
Why would I hurt Florence?

561
00:42:19,540 --> 00:42:23,043
I know why you did that earlier.

562
00:42:23,043 --> 00:42:25,746
You're trying to use Florence
to hurt Antonia.

563
00:42:25,746 --> 00:42:29,780
First chance you get, you better cut it off.

564
00:42:29,780 --> 00:42:32,200
Stop pretending like she's your girlfriend,

565
00:42:32,200 --> 00:42:34,500
before someone gets hurt.

566
00:42:51,071 --> 00:42:55,087
Shall we, my Chummy pie?
